# Build context for Dockerfile.cloudrun is the REPOSITORY ROOT, because that
# image needs both calmsense-backend/ and admin-app/.
#
# Docker only reads the .dockerignore at the root of the build context, so
# calmsense-backend/.dockerignore and admin-app/.dockerignore are NOT applied
# to that build. This file is what actually protects it. Without it the image
# would contain a live admin password hash (calmsense-backend/data/
# admin_users.json) and 50+ MB of host node_modules holding win32 binaries
# that break the Linux Vite build.
#
# Keep in sync with .gcloudignore, which does the same job for the upload when
# deploying with `gcloud run deploy --source .`.

# --- version control / tooling ---
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/

# --- dependency and build output (must be rebuilt inside the image) ---
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.venv/
**/venv/
admin-app/dist/
android-app/

# --- secrets and local state ---
# .env files hold the Supabase service_role key; data/ holds real user data
# and the admin password hash. Neither belongs in an image layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
calmsense-backend/data/
*.tgz

# --- not needed at runtime ---
# Dev-only scripts and Windows launchers.
**/*.bat
update-server.sh
scripts/
samsung-partner/
generated imagery/
*.pdf
*.docx
*.png
*.jpg
**/README.md
!admin-app/README.md
